fact WorkItem(id: "WI-1117", description: some(value: "anthill-todo backend, INCREMENT 5 of WI-437: SYNC. Design: backend-github-coordination.md §6.3, §6.4, §7.2, §7.3, §7.4, §10; §14 row 5. Ships the mirror and both return channels; it is what closes the autonomous-mode loop. GOVERNING PRINCIPLE THROUGHOUT: every datum has exactly ONE writable home. Sync is RECONCILIATION, NOT WRITE-THROUGH (§7.2) -- the tree is the truth, the issue is a projection, and mirrored state is never read back (§13). Work: (1) PROVISIONAL-ID RECONCILIATION (§6.4): allocate a permanent id for each WI-t<6hex> item, rename its file, and rewrite every depends_on reference to it. (2) ALLOCATION-DEBRIS REPAIR (§6.3): the states a lost or crashed stake can leave behind. (3) THE MIRROR PUSH (§7.1-§7.2): issue title and body derived from the item. (4) COMMENT INGESTION (§7.3): issue comments come back as Feedback facts with author `github:<login>`, ingested ONCE keyed on (workitem, author, at) so re-running is monotone-compatible (proposal 053); comments sync itself authored carry an `[anthill-todo sync]` marker and are skipped, so the channel does not echo. This is not bidirectional sync of mirrored state: comments have one writable home (GitHub), tracker state has one (the tree), and neither writes the other's. (5) CLOSE-AS-VERIFY (§7.4): closing a Delivered item's issue is a VERIFY GESTURE -- an event, not state, honored in that one legal transition and then re-derived. A close in any other status is DRIFT: reopen it and report. A reopen of a terminal item is likewise drift. (6) DELETION TOMBSTONES. (7) `--check` mode plus the CI gate, and the §10 loud-failure checks. ACCESS CONFIGURATION (§3, §6.4): GithubAccess is the project-wide DEFAULT, overridden per checkout by ANTHILL_TODO_GITHUB=on|off or --offline -- for CI test jobs, air-gapped machines, and fork checkouts without write access. Related but separate: WI-697 (timeout autoverify) is the fully-autonomous sibling of §7.4."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-1122"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Open)

fact Tag(workitem: "WI-1117", name: "wi437")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-1117", author: "user", content: "SCOPE NARROWED 2026-08-17 -- READ BEFORE CLAIMING. The continuously reconciled mirror is now a FUTURE EXTENSION; what this ticket ships is EXPORT and IMPORT (design §7, amended).\n\n  export -- write the tracker's current state to the target. Idempotent, keyed by MirrorEntry, and UNCONDITIONALLY TRACKER-WINS.\n  import -- pull comments back in as Feedback, for review before they land.\n\nWHAT COLLAPSES, and it is most of §7. §7.2's 'reconciliation, not write-through' exists because sync tried to be bidirectional-ish; export has ONE direction, settled, so reconciliation becomes a loop that overwrites. §7.4's close-as-verify -- an EVENT honoured in exactly one legal transition and re-derived otherwise, with a drift report for every other case -- collapses entirely. §10's 'permanent-id item with no MirrorEntry' check goes with it, since export creates the link as it goes and there is no continuous invariant to violate. §7.3's ingest-once bookkeeping softens to a cheap dedup on (author, at), because import is REVIEWED rather than automatic. Deletion tombstones, --check and the CI gate all belong to the future extension, not here.\n\nWHAT IT COSTS is that a reader sees the last export, not live state. Running export from CI on main recovers most of that FOR FREE -- precisely because it is idempotent and tracker-wins, so there is no drift machinery to get wrong.\n\nMirrorEntry MOVED HERE from the retired WI-1116, and its shape changed twice as a consequence of retiring §6.1:\n  entity MirrorEntry(workitem: String, target: String, entry: String)\n  * entry is a STRING, not Int64. The draft required a number because §6.1's soundness rested on identifiers TOTALLY ORDERED BY CREATION. With the allocator gone the external id is an opaque handle and must be -- a Jira key is PROJ-123, a Linear id is a ULID, a URL is a URL. Requiring a counter would exclude every target that is not a forge.\n  * target says WHICH external system. Implicit while there was one GitHub repo; cannot stay implicit now that an item's external ids are a SET.\nAN ITEM'S EXTERNAL IDS ARE A SET AND THE RELATIONAL FORM ALREADY IS ONE: N MirrorEntry facts for one item is N rows, exactly how Tag gives an item a set of tags. No list field, no schema change, no Option nesting. It stays OUT of the WorkItem entity -- a field there would read none in 1110 of 1112 items and would put a mirror concern in the stage0 domain.\n\nCONFIG RENAMED: fact Coordination is now fact Mirror(target: Term, access: MirrorAccess), with no allocation field (one policy is not a seam) and no Option on target (an ABSENT fact means no mirror). The field is target rather than forge because an export target need not be a forge -- Jira, Linear, a static site or a directory of files can all be one.", at: "2026-08-17T09:45:34Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-1117", author: "user", content: "ABSORBS WI-1115's REMAINING HALF 2026-08-17. WI-1115 is split: its substrate half became WI-1122 (embedder-supplied host functions, an anthill-core seam this ticket now depends on), and its carrier half lands HERE, because export/import is its only consumer.\n\nSO THIS TICKET ALSO SHIPS: the Forge carrier sort and its contract, the provides/operation_map bindings, and two implementations -- one shelling out to gh (inheriting the user's existing auth, no token handling of our own) and one fake over an in-memory list so export/import is testable without a network.\n\nTHE OPERATION SET IS SMALL NOW, and smaller than §8.3's list: create/update an entry, list entries, list comments. NOT fresh_token (ids are minted locally and purely -- no entropy source needed), NOT retitle, NOT close/reopen-for-retreat, NOT entries_titled -- those four were §6.1's allocator machinery and went with WI-1116.\n\nTHE FAKE'S JOB CHANGED TOO. §8.3 justified it as a first-class seam that could force §6.1's lost-race interleavings deterministically and let tests search whole schedule spaces under Branch (027.2 solvers, asserting no duplicate ids across every branch). There is no race left, so there is no schedule space: the fake now exists simply so export and import can be tested offline. Worth knowing before over-engineering it.\n\nDEPENDENCY ADDED ON WI-1122: without the embedder host-fn seam an operation_map naming gh_create_entry is not constructible, so the carrier cannot be bound at all.", at: "2026-08-17T10:36:43Z")
